00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.620
When they first collide, they're evenly matched,

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:35.160
in identical armor, wielding identical weapons,

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:37.460
even making identical fight moves.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:40.140
It isn't until a newly socially intelligent Shinji

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:42.340
breaks the cycle of combat and tries to connect

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.960
with his father that they make any progress.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:50.150
Here, Shinji finally understands the motivations

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:53.540
behind his dad's extremely ambitious and impractical plan.

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:57.670
That is, the pain of losing his wife, Shinji's mom.

00:14:57.670 --> 00:15:00.000
The pain caused by this emotional fracture leads

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.060
Gendo to try and annihilate something that's essentially human, his selfhood, and that of

00:15:05.060 --> 00:15:10.210
every other human on Earth. Rather than taking a note from Kierkegaard and bravely accepting his

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:15.430
internal fractures and trying to live a meaningful life, he's simply trying to kill that difference.

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:22.050
It's both kind of rational and also completely f***ing bad s***. And ultimately, it's not the

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:26.670
ambition of his project that stops Gendo. It's finally connecting with another human.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:30.000
Ironically, the man who was fighting

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.260
to artificially connect all of humanity

00:15:32.260 --> 00:15:35.220
really just needed to go to therapy with his emo son.

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.520
After connecting with Shinji and achieving closure,

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:40.540
he can finally die and rejoin Shinji's mom

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:42.100
in some weird ether world.

00:15:42.490 --> 00:15:43.930
And what about Shinji?

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.990
He's confronted his internal demons

00:15:45.990 --> 00:15:47.770
and defeated slash freed his dad,

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:50.810
so what more could a whiny teenage boy ask for?

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:52.360
A girlfriend, obviously.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:54.640
After Mari appears to rescue him,

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.140
we jump into a future where Shinji,

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:58.180
for the first time ever, is an adult.

00:15:58.610 --> 00:16:00.000
and not only an adult,

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.460
but one who can talk and even flirt with Mari,

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:03.920
his apparent partner.

00:16:03.920 --> 00:16:06.380
Here, he's done what Kierkegaard never could,

00:16:06.380 --> 00:16:09.950
namely finding happiness, and of course, a girlfriend.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:11.570
Once Shinji took the leap of faith

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.310
and found a truth he could care about,

00:16:13.310 --> 00:16:16.560
he grew up and moved on to the next stage of his life.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:19.420
Which brings us to one last element of the story.

00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:21.040
You might've noticed there's an EVA pilot

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.270
we haven't mentioned yet, Kaoru.

00:16:23.270 --> 00:16:25.270
He plays many roles in the story,

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:27.550
helping Shinji start to learn to be confident,

00:16:27.550 --> 00:16:30.000
introducing him to music, functioning as a homo

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.630
erotic love interest and accidentally almost bringing

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:34.120
about the end of the world.

00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:37.880
This happens a lot, but for us, his most important moment

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:40.080
in the new movies is this line.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.400
See, at the end of the rebuild, it is revealed

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:46.300
that there have been many Kaoru's,

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:50.470
and it is heavily implied many Shinji's, Rei's, and Asuka's.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:51.990
It looks like everyone's been stuck

00:16:51.990 --> 00:16:53.970
in a good old fashioned time loop.

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.000
However, at the end

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.820
of thrice upon a time, Shinji has clearly moved on

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:06.080
to a whole new world of Mari, one free of Eva's.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.060
So what are we to make of this?

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.760
Well, there's a lot of ways to look at it,

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:12.300
but we think there's something meta going on here.

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:15.020
Hideaki Anno has long talked about how the ending

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:17.160
of "Evangelion" wasn't satisfying to him

00:17:17.160 --> 00:17:20.250
after the show and subsequent movies ran out of money.

00:17:20.250 --> 00:17:23.490
Not only that, but since the release of the original series,

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:26.770
he's been largely known as the guy who did "Evangelion."

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.620
That's in part because it was a great artistic achievement

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:30.000
but also the most important

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.120
also because it was a deeply personal piece of work

00:17:33.120 --> 00:17:35.120
through which Anno worked through his own feelings

00:17:35.120 --> 00:17:36.940
of depression and isolation,

00:17:36.940 --> 00:17:40.130
like a modern version of "A Certain Sad Dane."

00:17:40.130 --> 00:17:41.510
With both Shinji and Gendo

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:43.970
each breaking through the loop at the end of this film,

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:47.030
we can interpret this as Anno finally putting the series

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:49.740
to bed and being ready, just like them,

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:51.480
to move on to something new.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:52.900
That's also why it's fitting that,

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:55.330
as Mari and Shinji run out of the train station,

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.970
the movie concludes with some straight-up live-action shots

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:00.000
of the very town where

00:18:00.090 --> 00:18:01.460
Anno grew up.

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.420
Much like how Shinji finally escaped

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.380
from the spirals of teenage depression,

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:07.600
it seems that Anno can finally move on

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:09.340
from the magnificent project

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:11.950
that was Neon Genesis Evangelion.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:13.570
But what do you guys think?

